# The probe writes its report beside itself. A returned report carries a third party's machine identity
# and must pass a leak scan before anybody commits it, so it is ignored by default rather than staged by
# accident.
gpu-probe-report.txt
gpu-probe-report.json

# The snapshot writer renders each incremental report beside its target and renames it into place, so a
# process killed mid-write leaves the PREVIOUS snapshot rather than a truncated one. That window is the
# only time these two exist, and only a kill inside it leaves one behind.
gpu-probe-report.txt.writing
gpu-probe-report.json.writing
